WEBVTT

00:00:00.980 --> 00:00:03.280
Father... Mother...

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:25.930
Father! Mother!

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:36.140
<i>A dream...</i>

00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:14.180
<i>Why?</i>

00:01:15.930 --> 00:01:18.390
Why can't I solve them anymore?!

00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:42.180
Kimi no nounai e to shinnyuu
Gonna infiltrate your brain

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:44.910
Nemutteru suki ni baby, open the gate
While you're sleeping, baby, open the gate

00:01:44.910 --> 00:01:46.760
Fukuzatsusugi security
Too-complicated security

00:01:46.760 --> 00:01:49.500
Kakusareru to abakitakunaru
When something's hidden, it makes me want to expose it

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:54.010
Barabara ni chirabatte iru password o hiroiatsume
I'll gather up those loose, scattered passwords

00:01:54.010 --> 00:01:58.720
Kakushin ni sematte yuku, sono shoutai o misete
And approach the core, so show me that true form

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:00.940
Kantan ni clear dekinai
I can't clear it easily

00:02:00.940 --> 00:02:03.590
Saki nante motto yomenai
Can read what lies ahead even less

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:05.600
Kaidoku fukanou smile
A smile that can't be deciphered

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:07.900
Kiken na puzzle
A dangerous puzzle

00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:09.840
Lock sareteta door aru nara
If there's a door that's been locked

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:12.660
Zutto tataite miru beki, kaza-ana hiraku wa
You must keep striking it, a crack will open

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:17.160
Eien ni hodokenai nazo nanka wa nai
No mystery remains unsolved forever

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:19.460
Makiokosu, it's a supernova!
It's forming, it's a supernova!

00:02:19.460 --> 00:02:24.150
Tobikiri shigekiteki na hirameki o agemashou
I will give you thoroughly stimulating insight

00:02:24.150 --> 00:02:26.370
Misskey-misskey la-tu-ma

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:28.710
Yume no naka, it's a supernova!
In the middle of a dream, it's a supernova!

00:02:28.710 --> 00:02:31.340
Watashi wa, sou, brain diver
I am, yes, a brain diver

00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:37.230
Kimi ga sagashimotometeru kotae ni nareru made
Until I become familiar with the answer you seek

00:02:39.890 --> 00:02:42.910
Brain diver

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:47.710
Brain diver

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:56.340
Resurgence Toward the Light

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:05.190
And then, right?

00:03:05.190 --> 00:03:08.430
In PE class last time,
they said we could go all-out,

00:03:08.430 --> 00:03:11.970
so I went with a full-on reverse cross!

00:03:11.970 --> 00:03:14.570
And my teacher passed out!

00:03:19.390 --> 00:03:22.640
No reaction. My plan failed, huh?

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:24.950
Hey there, DaiMORON!

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:29.270
Dunce cap, your one saving
grace was doin' puzzles.

00:03:29.720 --> 00:03:31.630
If a puzzle-lovin' fool
stops lovin' puzzles,

00:03:31.630 --> 00:03:34.440
what does that make? One, two...

00:03:34.450 --> 00:03:37.940
Yes! A plain old fooooool...!

00:03:41.270 --> 00:03:42.400
Gammon!

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:45.000
Now listen! Try putting
yourself in Kaito's position!

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:46.760
Let go!

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:49.760
That don't... really bother me.

00:03:51.270 --> 00:03:54.960
I'm still gonna solve
those guys' puzzles.

00:03:55.560 --> 00:03:57.430
Puzzle of God, my ass.

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:00.660
What's with him?

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:03.480
I wonder if Kaito's all right.

00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:07.300
Cube!

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:15.820
I have to ANALYZE him...

00:04:15.820 --> 00:04:17.690
Huh?!

00:04:24.750 --> 00:04:26.450
Wh-Where am I?

00:04:26.450 --> 00:04:28.260
Oh, you're awake?

00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:30.200
Kaito, good morning.

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:35.460
The heck is this?!

00:04:35.990 --> 00:04:38.590
Hey! Let me go! Let me out!

00:04:38.590 --> 00:04:40.210
Just as I predicted.

00:04:42.290 --> 00:04:46.430
The Armlet of Orpheus
stimulates neural activity,

00:04:46.430 --> 00:04:49.600
awakening normally dormant abilities.

00:04:50.070 --> 00:04:51.050
But...

00:04:52.210 --> 00:04:55.990
In Kaito's case, something
more awesome is going on.

00:04:56.330 --> 00:04:57.520
"Awesome"?

00:04:57.950 --> 00:05:01.690
Yes. One hundred percent of the brain,

00:05:01.690 --> 00:05:03.070
even the area for emotions,

00:05:03.070 --> 00:05:06.240
was all being used for solving puzzles.

00:05:07.730 --> 00:05:08.910
Emotions?!

00:05:10.670 --> 00:05:13.540
That's why he seemed
like a different person.

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:20.530
But I, Ana, think holding in

00:05:20.530 --> 00:05:23.510
your feelings would make you explode.

00:05:23.510 --> 00:05:27.550
Yes. The result was
that counter-reaction.

00:05:28.340 --> 00:05:31.200
That was 100% of the brain

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:33.640
being controlled only by emotions.

00:05:38.850 --> 00:05:41.190
That's enough, right? Let me go.

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:43.390
Oh. Sorry.

00:05:48.490 --> 00:05:49.650
Those guys...

00:05:50.070 --> 00:05:51.430
Say, Kaito...

00:05:54.750 --> 00:05:55.860
What is it?

00:05:58.030 --> 00:06:00.540
You shouldn't solve puzzles anymore!

00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:03.300
Huh? Cube!

00:06:03.230 --> 00:06:04.860
It's dangerous.

00:06:04.860 --> 00:06:09.340
Stimulating the brain,
forcing it into activity...

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:13.760
If it caused another counter-reaction,
it could be deadly.

00:06:13.760 --> 00:06:14.310
Huh?

00:06:14.870 --> 00:06:17.920
Deadly? It can't be!

00:06:17.920 --> 00:06:19.890
The possibility is there.

00:06:19.890 --> 00:06:22.350
The brain is the body's nerve center.

00:06:23.050 --> 00:06:25.340
As long as that armlet is intact,

00:06:25.340 --> 00:06:28.570
it could cause another
counter-reaction at any time.

00:06:29.330 --> 00:06:30.610
For real?!

00:06:30.610 --> 00:06:31.570
No...

00:06:32.370 --> 00:06:36.330
You became unable to solve
puzzles because your brain

00:06:36.330 --> 00:06:38.790
sensed danger and is now resisting puzzles.

00:06:43.330 --> 00:06:44.390
The POG?

00:06:45.130 --> 00:06:46.190
Wait, Kaito!

00:06:46.190 --> 00:06:48.580
I don't have to use the
armlet's power, right?!

00:06:53.340 --> 00:06:57.930
I don't... I don't need some... armlet!

00:07:01.930 --> 00:07:04.270
Kaito! Kaito, are you okay?

00:07:04.770 --> 00:07:06.000
I knew it.

00:07:17.760 --> 00:07:19.040
I get it.

00:07:19.630 --> 00:07:21.920
You stay and get some rest, kiddy.

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:23.890
I'LL be taking this prize.

00:07:24.330 --> 00:07:26.800
Huh?! Screw that!

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:29.540
I'm gettin' those POG bastards!

00:07:29.540 --> 00:07:32.030
I'll solve ALL their puzzles-

00:07:32.030 --> 00:07:34.050
Your MOUTH is as active as ever!

00:07:34.490 --> 00:07:37.880
But if you can't solve a
simple-ass puzzle like this,

00:07:37.880 --> 00:07:39.330
just what is your plan?

00:07:39.330 --> 00:07:40.400
Well?!

00:07:43.560 --> 00:07:47.830
It seems the POG have again
moved to contact Kaito.

00:07:48.830 --> 00:07:51.330
As forceful as always, aren't they?

00:07:51.750 --> 00:07:56.710
Just what does the POG
want with him like THIS?

00:07:56.710 --> 00:07:58.870
At this rate, Kaito is...

00:07:58.870 --> 00:08:02.810
All we can do is watch over him.

00:08:04.580 --> 00:08:05.830
That's right!

00:08:06.260 --> 00:08:08.000
And when I opened the door...

00:08:09.090 --> 00:08:11.590
Puzzle Club

00:08:09.510 --> 00:08:11.340
Challenge me?!

00:08:11.590 --> 00:08:13.240
Interesting.

00:08:13.240 --> 00:08:16.100
You would challenge
ME, Takeda, yourself?!

00:08:16.710 --> 00:08:17.720
Try solving this!

00:08:17.720 --> 00:08:19.640
It's Mr. Takeda's latest sudoku puzz-

00:08:19.640 --> 00:08:20.600
Give it!

00:08:24.330 --> 00:08:28.360
Some... Some puzzle like this...!

00:08:38.800 --> 00:08:42.620
Wh... Wh-Wh-Wh-Wh-Wh-Wh-Wh-What?

00:08:43.240 --> 00:08:46.720
We... We... We...

00:08:46.720 --> 00:08:48.400
We did it!

00:08:48.400 --> 00:08:49.790
I finally won!

00:08:49.790 --> 00:08:51.630
Congratulations, Mr. Takeda!

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:53.890
Yes! You're Einstein Takeda!

00:08:53.890 --> 00:08:56.990
"Genius is 99% perspiration"!

00:08:56.990 --> 00:08:58.410
EDISON said that!

00:08:58.330 --> 00:09:00.410
Oh? Really?!

00:09:00.410 --> 00:09:03.250
Strike a pose, Einstein!
Ba-baam! Ba-baam!

00:09:19.550 --> 00:09:21.410
I heard!

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:23.600
Gammon.

00:09:24.720 --> 00:09:27.180
Looks like "Einstein" lost to a couple

00:09:27.180 --> 00:09:29.270
of dudes from the Puzzle Club.

00:09:30.360 --> 00:09:31.450
Shut up.

00:09:31.450 --> 00:09:32.950
Here.

00:09:33.780 --> 00:09:37.800
"7:00 pm, Oni-no-kuchi
Shrine, I'll be waiting."

00:09:33.780 --> 00:09:37.800
[Oni-no-kuchi: Devil's Mouth]

00:09:38.470 --> 00:09:40.550
That's what the code from before said.

00:09:41.220 --> 00:09:44.550
They hit the keyboard toggle key between
Japanese and English.

00:09:44.550 --> 00:09:46.500
A piss-poor level of a puzzle.

00:09:45.210 --> 00:09:48.040
7:00 pm  Oni-no-kuchi Shrine
I'll be waiting

00:09:48.620 --> 00:09:51.330
To think you couldn't even solve THAT...

00:09:53.060 --> 00:09:55.320
See ya. I'm goin'.

00:09:55.320 --> 00:09:56.450
Wait!

00:09:56.950 --> 00:09:58.660
Don't get full of yourself.

00:09:59.020 --> 00:10:00.910
There's no way I'm lettin' YOU go!

00:10:00.910 --> 00:10:02.030
Shut up!

00:10:05.260 --> 00:10:07.620
Now who's gettin' full of himself?!

00:10:09.250 --> 00:10:11.340
You piss me off.

00:10:11.680 --> 00:10:14.510
You think you're special, don't you?

00:10:15.740 --> 00:10:18.010
Don't ever show your face to me again.

00:10:20.180 --> 00:10:21.800
Hey, wait!

00:10:21.800 --> 00:10:23.790
Gammon! Don't play deaf!

00:10:24.630 --> 00:10:27.020
I'm the one who solves puzzles!

00:10:27.720 --> 00:10:29.020
ME!

00:10:29.320 --> 00:10:30.810
I am!

00:10:51.640 --> 00:10:55.130
Engulfed by his own memories,
his body broken...

00:10:55.550 --> 00:10:59.280
Why extend another invitation
to Kaito Daimon?

00:11:07.670 --> 00:11:09.390
I want to see it.

00:11:10.040 --> 00:11:13.290
That which lies ahead...

00:11:23.210 --> 00:11:24.280
Kaito.

00:11:26.550 --> 00:11:28.870
I thought you'd be here.

00:11:31.620 --> 00:11:33.310
You remembered, didn't you?

00:11:34.030 --> 00:11:36.020
About your father and mother.

00:11:36.720 --> 00:11:39.170
I ain't never forgotten
about them, not once.

00:11:39.170 --> 00:11:43.340
Puzzles and that man saved
me from bein' alone.

00:11:44.610 --> 00:11:45.930
So I thought.

00:11:51.310 --> 00:11:53.000
Kaito, I know...

00:11:55.760 --> 00:11:59.330
I know how important puzzles are to you.

00:12:03.400 --> 00:12:07.470
But even if you can't solve puzzles,
you're still YOU, Kaito.

00:12:07.820 --> 00:12:08.700
You'll be fine!

00:12:09.290 --> 00:12:12.890
So if it's too rough, I think
you should quit puzzles.

00:12:13.830 --> 00:12:15.950
Quit puzzles?

00:12:26.860 --> 00:12:28.510
<i>Stupid puzzles.</i>

00:12:32.720 --> 00:12:33.650
<i>You fine with that?</i>

00:12:36.140 --> 00:12:37.710
<i>You really liked them, right?</i>

00:12:37.710 --> 00:12:39.440
You're okay with giving them up?

00:12:40.240 --> 00:12:42.190
<i>Even if you do, you can't escape</i>

00:12:42.190 --> 00:12:45.820
<i>
the sadness of having lost something dear.</i>

00:12:47.250 --> 00:12:49.350
<i>Don't give up what is dear.</i>

00:12:50.830 --> 00:12:52.270
<i>Never.</i>

00:12:56.030 --> 00:12:57.050
I...

00:12:59.240 --> 00:13:00.120
Kaito?

00:13:00.700 --> 00:13:01.860
I have to go.

00:13:02.830 --> 00:13:03.590
Hey!

00:13:03.930 --> 00:13:04.970
You can't go!

00:13:05.280 --> 00:13:07.970
He said it could be deadly!

00:13:07.970 --> 00:13:09.470
I made a promise!

00:13:10.260 --> 00:13:12.310
Wait, Kaito!

00:13:12.980 --> 00:13:15.140
Puzzle time... Let's begin!

00:13:16.720 --> 00:13:18.320
Darn it, Kaito!

00:13:28.680 --> 00:13:32.230
It's almost time, huh?

00:13:50.920 --> 00:13:52.350
Welcome...

00:13:52.880 --> 00:13:55.220
...to Oni-no-kuchi Shrine.

00:13:55.240 --> 00:13:57.850
So you're the Giver this time, huh?

00:13:58.480 --> 00:14:01.860
You are not the pact holder
with the Armlet of Orpheus.

00:14:02.750 --> 00:14:04.750
Where is he of the Armlet?

00:14:04.750 --> 00:14:06.500
I will solve your puzzle.

00:14:07.440 --> 00:14:09.110
He fled from fear, did he?

00:14:10.180 --> 00:14:11.620
That ain't it at all.

00:14:12.620 --> 00:14:14.120
How foolish.

00:14:16.180 --> 00:14:17.260
A kid?!

00:14:18.360 --> 00:14:20.380
Demons shall feed upon you.

00:14:20.930 --> 00:14:23.380
For I am the devil's handmaiden.

00:14:23.380 --> 00:14:24.270
Wait!

00:14:27.460 --> 00:14:29.890
I was almost late for puzzle time.

00:14:31.260 --> 00:14:32.260
Kaito.

00:14:32.790 --> 00:14:34.770
I'LL be the one to solve your puzzle!

00:14:35.290 --> 00:14:39.020
Sheeit! Now you're here, I
guess it can't be helped.

00:14:39.920 --> 00:14:41.900
Don't be gettin' in the way, though.

00:14:45.170 --> 00:14:48.110
It seems tonight's players
have all gathered.

00:14:48.660 --> 00:14:53.120
Once swallowed in the devil's mouth,
not one has emerged alive!

00:14:53.620 --> 00:14:55.120
That suits me fine!

00:15:10.920 --> 00:15:12.920
This is the devil's mouth?

00:15:12.920 --> 00:15:14.810
Okay. Let's go.

00:15:18.270 --> 00:15:20.310
Welcome...

00:15:20.310 --> 00:15:22.470
To the belly of the devil.

00:15:22.940 --> 00:15:26.190
The puzzle you must
release lies before you.

00:15:35.980 --> 00:15:40.330
Insert characters into the
six blanks and make a circle.

00:15:41.180 --> 00:15:44.790
You shall enter six of
these seven characters.

00:15:44.790 --> 00:15:47.820
They will form above the unused character.

00:15:47.820 --> 00:15:52.780
Do this, and you shall be
guided toward the prize.

00:15:53.890 --> 00:15:54.850
I'll solve it.

00:16:00.100 --> 00:16:01.030
Kaito?

00:16:01.370 --> 00:16:03.460
Damn. He's no good, huh?

00:16:07.360 --> 00:16:14.210
Stick six of the seven characters
into the blanks, huh?

00:16:15.970 --> 00:16:19.720
<i>Bubble... Bubble... Bubble... Done.</i>

00:16:20.200 --> 00:16:21.370
I get it.

00:16:22.170 --> 00:16:24.510
All these characters are
made up of two parts,

00:16:24.510 --> 00:16:26.880
one on the left and one on the right.

00:16:26.880 --> 00:16:31.150
And they all have similar elements.

00:16:31.690 --> 00:16:36.850
Rather, each character shares an element
with the previous one!

00:16:38.160 --> 00:16:40.950
So the character left behind is...

00:16:43.970 --> 00:16:45.240
NAWA!

00:16:45.870 --> 00:16:48.340
Yo! That was freakin' easy.

00:16:49.040 --> 00:16:50.150
A puzzle like this...

00:16:54.970 --> 00:16:55.910
The heck?!

00:16:57.160 --> 00:16:59.260
NAWA backwards is...

00:17:01.450 --> 00:17:02.290
NAWA...

00:17:03.220 --> 00:17:04.420
WANA!

00:17:09.180 --> 00:17:10.260
Gammon!

00:17:11.230 --> 00:17:12.170
Gammon!

00:17:12.200 --> 00:17:13.270
Nonoha!

00:17:17.890 --> 00:17:20.930
Nonoha! Just let go! At
this rate, you'll...!

00:17:20.930 --> 00:17:23.180
I can't do that, can I?

00:17:25.150 --> 00:17:27.020
Good! Very good!

00:17:27.480 --> 00:17:28.270
Dammit!

00:17:30.270 --> 00:17:34.210
In this world, the most revered
of prizes is human life!

00:17:34.900 --> 00:17:36.880
Do you not think so?

00:17:43.690 --> 00:17:46.420
This is a true Philosopher's Puzzle!

00:17:46.420 --> 00:17:50.260
If the two of you can
save yourselves, you win.

00:17:51.180 --> 00:17:52.820
But if you lose...

00:17:55.710 --> 00:17:57.210
Bitch!

00:18:00.920 --> 00:18:04.390
I wonder if you can escape
the maze of your own memories...

00:18:04.990 --> 00:18:06.430
Kaito Daimon.

00:18:07.840 --> 00:18:13.320
Well? If you don't hurry,
your most valued "prizes" will disappear.

00:18:15.140 --> 00:18:16.820
<i>I won't let it. </i>

00:18:16.820 --> 00:18:19.910
<i>This piece-of-shit puzzle...
I WILL solve it!</i>

00:18:20.660 --> 00:18:25.830
Insert characters into the
six blanks and make a circle.

00:18:25.830 --> 00:18:31.400
The symmetry of nature's power
will no doubt grant your wishes.

00:18:32.190 --> 00:18:34.780
"Nature's power"? What's that?

00:18:34.780 --> 00:18:37.420
Dammit! Which should I choose?

00:18:37.420 --> 00:18:39.260
Kaito!

00:18:39.680 --> 00:18:41.510
Nonoha! That's enough!

00:18:41.510 --> 00:18:42.820
Just let go!

00:18:42.820 --> 00:18:44.010
No!

00:18:55.380 --> 00:18:56.720
I...!

00:18:58.070 --> 00:18:59.530
A counter-reaction!

00:19:00.030 --> 00:19:01.020
What should we do?

00:19:01.020 --> 00:19:02.030
Kaito...

00:19:02.210 --> 00:19:04.170
Kaito will break!

00:19:04.750 --> 00:19:07.680
I-I...

00:19:09.720 --> 00:19:12.480
Don't give up on what is dear.

00:19:16.910 --> 00:19:19.550
I... I won't run.

00:19:20.130 --> 00:19:23.550
I will solve this puzzle!

00:19:34.500 --> 00:19:35.580
Don't tell me...!

00:19:43.250 --> 00:19:46.240
In this order, the characters
form a magic hexagon.

00:19:48.040 --> 00:19:51.520
Nature's power is contained
in these characters.

00:19:51.520 --> 00:19:54.040
Water, earth...

00:19:54.040 --> 00:19:56.370
Fire, wood...

00:19:56.760 --> 00:19:58.410
Four elements.

00:20:06.360 --> 00:20:10.660
In other words, I should
arrange the characters so that

00:20:10.660 --> 00:20:12.560
all left-side parts correspond to these four things.

00:20:15.730 --> 00:20:17.480
The wood elements go here.

00:20:18.240 --> 00:20:20.690
And then the fire elements, here.

00:20:21.130 --> 00:20:22.840
Two circles left.

00:20:22.840 --> 00:20:25.520
The two elements relating to these are...

00:20:28.160 --> 00:20:29.290
Solved it.

00:20:29.560 --> 00:20:30.500
What?

00:20:45.260 --> 00:20:47.260
Uh... Huh?

00:20:50.850 --> 00:20:52.120
We're saved.

00:21:01.950 --> 00:21:03.050
Kaito!

00:21:03.050 --> 00:21:07.410
It can't be. The devil's mouth...

00:21:13.650 --> 00:21:15.310
Say, Gammon...

00:21:16.640 --> 00:21:19.590
Will Kaito be okay?

00:21:20.670 --> 00:21:22.150
Guess it can't be helped:

00:21:23.000 --> 00:21:24.760
Nonoha sweets.

00:21:25.680 --> 00:21:27.560
Anything but that!

00:21:27.560 --> 00:21:29.640
Oh, thanks goodness!

00:21:31.390 --> 00:21:34.630
Sheeit! You're nothin' but a bother!

00:21:36.110 --> 00:21:37.530
Well, sorry.

00:21:39.910 --> 00:21:41.190
I'm grateful.

00:21:42.770 --> 00:21:46.000
A-All that happened is
your dumb ass got better!

00:21:46.000 --> 00:21:48.010
That's nothin' to say you're grateful about!

00:21:49.170 --> 00:21:51.950
You'd have been better off
bein' dumb forever, DaiMORON!

00:21:51.950 --> 00:21:53.040
What was that?!

00:21:53.040 --> 00:21:54.910
You're the guy who looked like a jackass

00:21:54.910 --> 00:21:56.880
as he felt right into a trap, Jackassamon!

00:21:56.880 --> 00:21:59.180
Who're you callin' Jackassamon?!
Say that again!

00:21:59.180 --> 00:22:01.130
I'll say it over and over, Jackassamon!

00:22:00.410 --> 00:22:02.550
You guys sure get along...

00:22:01.130 --> 00:22:02.860
Oh! Now you've said it twice!

00:22:02.860 --> 00:22:04.260
LIKE HELL!

00:22:06.870 --> 00:22:08.260
So, once again...

00:22:08.700 --> 00:22:12.260
He's taken a step toward
being a Phi-Brain, has he?

00:22:12.880 --> 00:22:14.020
Yes.

00:22:14.770 --> 00:22:18.090
And beyond that lies the Puzzle of God.

00:22:19.200 --> 00:22:24.880
You truly are dashing when
you're solving puzzles, Kaito Daimon.

00:22:34.580 --> 00:22:38.800
Tsukue no ue de umareta sekai
A world born on top of a desk

00:22:38.800 --> 00:22:44.720
Ichiban saki ni kimi ni misetakatta
I wanted to show it to you first of all

00:22:44.720 --> 00:22:49.350
Karappo no heya sotto nukedashite
I sneaked silently out of that empty room

00:22:49.350 --> 00:22:54.400
Hashirihajimeteta
And started running

00:22:55.560 --> 00:22:59.880
Iki hazumasete oka o noboru to
Breathing heavily, I climbed the hill

00:22:59.880 --> 00:23:05.240
Kimi ga saki ni tsuite matte ita ne
And you were already there, waiting

00:23:06.110 --> 00:23:10.420
Takusan no hajimete kimi to mitsuketa
There were so many treasures that I first

00:23:10.420 --> 00:23:15.670
Takaramono datta
Discovered with you

00:23:15.670 --> 00:23:21.010
Kanashisa de afureta toki wa
That time when I was overcome with sadness

00:23:21.010 --> 00:23:23.690
Nanimo iwazu ni tada
You said nothing

00:23:23.690 --> 00:23:26.600
Soba ni ite kureta ne
Just stayed there by my side, didn't you?

00:23:26.600 --> 00:23:31.170
Imademo wasurenai yo
Even now, I haven't forgotten

00:23:31.170 --> 00:23:36.470
Mata aou ne, yakusoku o shiyou
Let's meet again, let's make it a promise

00:23:36.470 --> 00:23:41.750
Kei wa shinai, ano hi no sayonara
It won't fade, the "goodbye" of that day

00:23:41.750 --> 00:23:47.290
Boku no subete, kimi ga kureta michi
Everything I have, the path you gave me

00:23:47.290 --> 00:23:56.230
Zutto kokoro no naka hikaru yo
Will always shine within my heart

00:24:01.190 --> 00:24:03.990
Love letters sure get
the blood racing, huh?

00:24:03.990 --> 00:24:05.660
I ain't really interested in 'em.

00:24:05.660 --> 00:24:09.260
By the shoe lockers after class
or slipped into your desk...

00:24:09.260 --> 00:24:11.260
You've never gotten one, have you?

00:24:11.260 --> 00:24:12.590
Yeah, just once.

00:24:12.590 --> 00:24:14.410
Huh? The heck?! What was it like?

00:24:14.410 --> 00:24:18.170
Mm, it was written in a
Mayan arithmetic code...

00:24:18.170 --> 00:24:20.690
It was way too easy for me.

00:24:19.910 --> 00:24:24.750
Nonoha's Title

00:24:20.690 --> 00:24:23.200
Next time: "Nonoha's Title"

00:24:23.200 --> 00:24:24.480
Scary, isn't it?
